record.description:
An upgrade guide for 1.0, since one change in it needs the operator before the first scheduled backup after the upgrade: every target now requires TLS (#44).

`docs/upgrading-to-1.0.md` covers:

* before: backing up the metadata database (Flyway only goes forward), checking which database servers speak TLS, with one command per engine, and letting running jobs finish;
* the upgrade itself, and what migration `V14` does to existing targets;
* after: testing every target, opting out the ones whose server cannot be given TLS yet, and checking one backup;
* what else is new and needs nothing (metrics, the Vietnamese console, the licence report, the additive `tlsRequired` API field, dbvault-cli 1.0);
* going back to 0.3 from the metadata dump.

`docs/README.md` lists it. Documentation only.
